# Workstation secrets (ADR-0013 class 3): what `bash scripts/setup.sh infra` fetches from Secret Manager.
# One per line: <secret name> <path>, e.g. `some-tool-token .env.some-tool`. The path is always .env.<name> at the
# repo's top (lower-case letters, digits and -; git-ignored by .env.*), never .env or .env.example. The file gets
# mode 600; its value is never printed.
